# Mismatches that are understood.  Anything NOT listed here fails the
# run; this file is the difference between a check and a tool that
# always says no.
#
# Format:  <file>:<name> <tab> reason
#
# KEYED BY FILE, not by name alone.  It was keyed by name, and one entry
# written about os/inferno/port/devdynld.c silently excused the same
# mismatch in emu/port/devdynldx.c -- a second file, in a different
# build, that nobody had looked at.  A baseline that over-matches is the
# same defect as a check that cannot fail.
#
# Each line is a claim someone verified.  Re-verify before adding one.
os/inferno/port/lib.h:log	devbench.c defines a kernel logger log(char*, ...) at file scope while lib.h declares libc's double log(double).  A NAME COLLISION between two different functions, not a miscounted call: nothing calls log() expecting the maths function in a kernel that links devbench.o.  The fix is to rename the logger, which is a change to devbench.c and not to this tool.
